id: pm-namespace-recovery-delivery
title: Deliver unambiguous registry-derived namespace recovery across installed Node and Bun consumers
description: "Execution child of the canonical recovery feature for GH-1433. Derive a canonical help retry for a misplaced registered namespace suffix, refuse ambiguous or unavailable routes and preserve nonempty item/history bytes through real installed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers. The parent retains the complete recovery-census programme."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-10T18:34:13.033Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-10T20:57:07.751Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-10T20:57:07.032Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-10T20:57:07.032Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Public SDK resolver uses installed canonical identity and refuses ambiguity; CLI JSON and text recommend inspection while preserving usage failure; real nonempty source and packed npx/bunx controls preserve authoritative bytes; existing discovery behavior and generated surface gates remain intact
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make a refused namespace mistake recoverable without guessing or executing a mutation
value: Agents discover the intended registered command from a concise executable refusal
why_now: Published 2026.10.10 reproducibly omits canonical update help for item update
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Normalize explicit tracker selection through the SDK to an absolute root, preserve complete refused paths and the selected extension registry, honor suppression, and verify equivalent source/executable tokenized help recovery."
expected_result: "Canonical inspection replays against the selected tracker from another cwd/default tracker, leaves authoritative bytes unchanged, and agrees between SDK source and installed executables. Merge requires exact 100 percent coverage of the final head."
actual_result: "All 18 linked tests pass including source/executable parity, relative tracker selection and replay from a different cwd. Packed npx and bunx relative-path recovery passes for 9 packages. The prior head CI exposed exactly one scoped-retry branch not instrumented by subprocess tests; the added source parity path exercises it. Existing complete static, 199 measurement tests and SDK consumer proofs are retained; fresh exact final-head CI coverage/review is mandatory before merge."
